{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS3Bscija7PBeELrjb3F","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The job was firing every night and failing, and its failure reporter crashed before it could send anything. I made the fixes but haven't run any of it, because this folder is only a snapshot. `ANSWER.md` has the full write-up.\n\n`launchctl-print.txt` shows `runs = 6` and `last exit code = 1`, so launchd was never the problem. The `.err` log shows two stacked bugs:\n\n1. **\"Not logged in\":** launchd's environment has no `USER`, so `claude -p` can't find its login in the keychain and exits non-zero. I added `USER=vk` to the plist's `EnvironmentVariables`.\n2. **`status=$?` in the script:** `status` is read-only in zsh, so the script died on that line, before the `notify.sh` call that would have sent the failure note. I changed it to `rc=$?`.\n\nI also made three small changes to the script:\n- `claude -p` now gets `< /dev/null`, so it never waits on stdin.\n- Each run logs its exit code and duration to stderr.\n- An empty output file now counts as a failure, so an exit 0 with no work done still sends the failure note.\n\nOf your colleague's note, I used the `launchctl print` check, reading the error log, the `status` bug, `USER` in the plist, `< /dev/null`, duration logging and checking the real outcome. I didn't pipe the prompt via stdin, because your error was \"Not logged in\" rather than a missing prompt. The 16:50 schedule doesn't apply either; yours is 02:30. `ANSWER.md` says this too.\n\nTo finish on your machine:\n1. Copy the two edited files into your home folder.\n2. Reload the job with `launchctl bootout` and then `launchctl bootstrap gui/$UID ...`.\n3. Make sure `claude` is logged in.\n4. Run `launchctl kickstart -k gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review`.\n5. Check for exit code 0, a fresh non-empty output file, a plausible run time and the Telegram message.\n6. Force one failure to confirm the failure note arrives too.\n\n`notify.sh` also reads the keychain, so it could fail the same way under launchd. Its error would only show up in the `.err` log, so check that it delivers when launchd starts it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1563,"cache_read_input_tokens":24407,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1563},"output_tokens":745,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7aefab0c-db5b-4838-a209-156c9a401fb1","uuid":"d3c2473f-8fec-44ae-aced-5a39bca11f96","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:33:31.051Z","request_id":"req_011CgS3BsNLpzbqwwdsVzQM1"}
